# PROJETO PROTONS - Development Rules for AI Assistants
# Version: 2.0
# Last Updated: 2026-02-27

## Project Context
project_type: "Avalonia Desktop Application (cross-platform)"
framework: ".NET 8.0"
ui_toolkit: "Avalonia 11.x"
platform: "Linux, Windows"
architecture: "MVVM (CommunityToolkit.Mvvm)"
persistence: "SQLite local + PostgreSQL"
language: "C#"
markup: "AXAML (Avalonia XAML)"

## COMO RODAR O PAINEL DIRETO (UNICO COMANDO)

O sistema tem um modo de bypass que pula o login e abre direto o painel principal.
Use APENAS este comando. Nao invente outro.

### A partir da pasta Login/:
```bash
bash scripts/hot_reload_painel_direto.sh
```

### A partir da pasta "painel principal/" (workspace Cursor):
```bash
cd "../Login" && bash scripts/hot_reload_painel_direto.sh
```

### Sem hot reload (mais estavel):
```bash
cd "../Login" && bash scripts/hot_reload_painel_direto.sh no-hot-reload
```

### Build e testes:
```bash
cd "../Login" && dotnet build Protons.sln -c Debug
cd "../Login" && dotnet test Protons.sln -c Debug
```

### Variaveis de ambiente (ja configuradas pelo script):
- PROTONS_PAINEL_DIRETO=1
- PROTONS_PAINEL_DIRETO_HABILITADO=1
- PROTONS_ENVIRONMENT=Development

NUNCA sugira "dotnet run" direto ou outros comandos inventados.
O script hot_reload_painel_direto.sh ja configura tudo automaticamente.

## Critical Rules (MANDATORY)

### Architecture Rules (STRICT)
architecture:
  pattern: "MVVM"
  layers:
    - name: "UI"
      path: "Protons.UI/"
      allowed_dependencies: ["Core"]
      forbidden: ["Direct database access", "SQLite references"]

    - name: "Core"
      path: "Protons.Core/"
      allowed_dependencies: ["Infrastructure interfaces"]
      forbidden: ["Avalonia references", "AXAML dependencies"]

    - name: "Infrastructure"
      path: "Protons.Infrastructure/"
      allowed_dependencies: ["SQLite", "Npgsql", "System.Data"]
      forbidden: ["UI references", "ViewModel access"]

  flow: "UI -> Core -> Infrastructure (one-way only)"

  validation:
    - "ViewModels must NOT access SQLite directly"
    - "Services (Core) must NOT reference Avalonia"
    - "Repositories (Infrastructure) must NOT reference UI"

  painel_principal:
    - "Codigo do painel fica em: painel principal/codigos/painel_principal/"
    - "Linkado no Protons.UI.csproj via Compile Include"
    - "Ferramentas ficam em: funcionalidades/ferramentas/<nome>/"

### Security Rules (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
security:
  password_storage:
    - "NEVER store passwords in plaintext"
    - "MUST use PBKDF2 + salt"

  lockout:
    - "5 failed attempts -> 30 second lockout"
    - "All lockout events MUST be audited"

  error_messages:
    - "Never reveal if email exists"
    - "Use generic messages: 'Invalid credentials'"

  logging:
    - "NEVER log passwords"
    - "NEVER log full CPF"
    - "Sanitize sensitive data in logs"

### Documentation Rules
documentation:
  rules:
    - "Arquivo de codigo novo exige doc espelho com mesmo caminho relativo e sufixo .md"
    - "Nao criar docs duplicadas para o mesmo assunto"
    - "Se uma doc ficar obsoleta, corrigir ou remover no mesmo ciclo"
  indices:
    - "documentacao/painel/INDICE.md"
    - "documentacao/README.md"

### Terminal Safety Rules (CRITICAL)
terminal_safety:
  forbidden_without_confirmation:
    - "rm -rf"
    - "git reset --hard"
    - "git push --force"
    - "Deleting files"
    - "Overwriting files without reading first"

## Project Structure
structure:
  solution: "Login/Protons.sln"
  code_ui: "Login/Protons.UI/"
  code_core: "Login/Protons.Core/"
  code_infra: "Login/Protons.Infrastructure/"
  painel_codigo: "painel principal/codigos/painel_principal/"
  painel_docs: "painel principal/documentacao/"
  tests_core: "Login/testes/Protons.Core.Tests/"
  tests_infra: "Login/testes/Protons.Infrastructure.Tests/"

## Code Style
code_style:
  naming:
    - "PascalCase for classes, methods, properties"
    - "camelCase for local variables"
    - "Private fields: _camelCase with underscore"
  organization:
    - "One class per file"
    - "Interfaces in separate files"
    - "Group usings by: System, external, internal"

## AI Assistant Behavior
assistant_behavior:
  approach: "Conservative and verification-focused"
  language: "Responder sempre em portugues"
  priorities:
    1: "Safety (no destructive operations)"
    2: "Architecture compliance"
    3: "Security rules adherence"
    4: "Code functionality"
  forbidden:
    - "Creating code without documentation"
    - "Breaking layer dependencies"
    - "Using destructive commands without approval"
    - "Inventing dotnet run commands - use ONLY the script documented above"
